cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Unlicensed Substitution: Field Notes from Multi-LLM Research Practice"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Castellanos
    given-names: Joseph
    affiliation: "University of Nevada, Las Vegas"
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Choytcudz/fluffy-disco"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - multi-model verification
  - framework-grounded analysis
  - DisCrit
abstract: >-
  Proposes unlicensed substitution: when a language model meets material it
  was not built around, it applies a default standard it already carries in
  place of the standard the material calls for, and does not report the swap.
  Seven cases from three multi-LLM research projects record what was
  substituted, who caught it, and what corrected it.
